#: new-start-29051/venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/git_filter_repo.py:1887
#: venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/git_filter_repo.py:1887
msgid "Parent rewriting"
msgstr ""

#: new-start-29051/venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/git_filter_repo.py:1892
#: venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/git_filter_repo.py:1892
msgid ""
"Replace refs (see git-replace(1)) are used to rewrite parents (unless "
"turned off by the usual git mechanism); this flag specifies what do do "
"with those refs afterward. Replace refs can either be deleted or updated "
"to point at new commit hashes.  Also, new replace refs can be added for "
"each commit rewrite.  With 'update-or-add', new replace refs are only "
"added for commit rewrites that aren't used to update an existing replace "
"ref. default is 'update-and-add' if $GIT_DIR/filter-repo/already_ran does"
" not exist; 'update-or-add' otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: new-start-29051/venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/git_filter_repo.py:1904
#: venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/git_filter_repo.py:1904
msgid ""
"Whether to prune empty commits.  'auto' (the default) means only prune "
"commits which become empty (not commits which were empty in the original "
"repo, unless their parent was pruned). When the parent of a commit is "
"pruned, the first non-pruned ancestor becomes the new parent."
msgstr ""

#: new-start-29051/venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/git_filter_repo.py:1911
#: venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/git_filter_repo.py:1911
msgid ""
"Since merge commits are needed for history topology, they are typically "
"exempt from pruning.  However, they can become degenerate with the "
"pruning of other commits (having fewer than two parents, having one "
"commit serve as both parents, or having one parent as the ancestor of the"
" other.)  If such merge commits have no file changes, they can be pruned."
"  The default ('auto') is to only prune empty merge commits which become "
"degenerate (not which started as such)."
msgstr ""

#: new-start-29051/venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/git_filter_repo.py:1920
#: venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/git_filter_repo.py:1920
msgid ""
"Even if the first parent is or becomes an ancestor of another parent, do "
"not prune it.  This modifies how --prune-degenerate behaves, and may be "
"useful in projects who always use merge --no-ff."
msgstr ""

